course: dictionary
lesson: 5197
title: Jail: a place, a verb, or a feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jail is a building where people are locked up as a punishment for a crime, or while they wait for a trial. As a verb, to jail someone means to put them into a jail. In the board game Monopoly, «Go to jail» means a player is sent to a jail space and must stay there for a while.
explain: Read the words around jail to find which meaning it has. «The town has a polar bear jail where bears are kept until they can be flown away.» Here jail is a building where animals are held. The clues are kept and until: a bear is held there for a time, just as a person is held in a real jail.
explain: Sometimes people use jail in a joking way. If someone says, «This rainy week in the tent feels like a jail», they do not mean a real prison. They mean a place where you cannot leave. Ask yourself: is a real building meant, or is it a feeling? The clues in the sentence will tell you.
explain: The word changes its shape. «Those men were jailed for stealing» uses the verb. In the Rat's words, «gaol-birds» means people who are often in prison, and gaol is an older spelling of jail. When you are not sure, check the dictionary.
fact: Jail is a noun when it names a building, and a verb when it means putting someone into one.
fact: «Jail» means a building where people are locked up as a punishment for crimes, or while they wait for trial.
fact: «Jailed» means put into jail, as in «jailed for» a crime.
fact: Gaol is an older spelling of jail, and a gaol-bird is someone who is often in prison.
fact: Informally, «jail» can mean any place where you feel you cannot leave.
exercise: «The town has a polar bear jail where bears are kept until they can be flown away.» What is a polar bear jail? | A bear's favourite place to hunt | *A place where bears are kept until they can be moved safely | A cold lake where bears swim | A toy shop for bears
exercise: «Those men were jailed for stealing from the bank.» What does jailed mean here? | Given a prize for being clever | *Put into jail as a punishment | Sent on a long holiday | Let out to play in the park
exercise: In the Rat's words, «gaol» is an old spelling of which modern word? | *jail | gold | goal | gull
test: «Ivy's strategy game has jails, police and income tax.» In this sentence, what is a jail? | A kind of crisp | A small park with a fence around it | *A place in a game where a player can be locked up for a time | A place in a game where a player can be locked up
test: Sam says, «My bedroom feels like a jail when I am stuck inside all day.» What does jail mean here? | A building with bars and guards | A park with lots of trees | A shop that sells toys | *Any place where you feel you cannot leave
exam: «He was jailed for three years.» What is the best meaning of jailed here? | Given three years of school | Asked to wait for a bus for three years | *Locked up in prison as a punishment for three years | Sent on a trip that lasted three years
